        "## **Setup Instructions for Local Environment**\n",
        "\n",
        "### **1. Install Dependencies**\n",
        "Make sure you have Python installed. You will need the following libraries: TensorFlow, Keras, NumPy, Matplotlib, Pillow, and Kaggle. You can install them using pip:\n",
        "```bash\n",
        "pip install tensorflow numpy matplotlib pillow kaggle\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "### **2. Download and Prepare the Dataset**\n",
        "This notebook uses the [Yoga Poses Dataset from Kaggle](https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/niharika41298/yoga-poses-dataset/data).\n",
        "\n",
        "**Using the Kaggle API:**\n",
        "1.  Ensure you have the Kaggle API installed (`pip install kaggle`).\n",
        "2.  Set up your Kaggle API credentials. Download your `kaggle.json` file from your Kaggle account page and place it in `~/.kaggle/` (Linux/macOS) or `C:\\Users\\<Your-Username>\\.kaggle\\` (Windows).\n",
        "3.  Download the dataset using the following command in your terminal. It's recommended to run this in the same directory where this notebook is located:\n",
        "    ```bash\n",
        "    kaggle datasets download -d niharika41298/yoga-poses-dataset\n",
        "    ```\n",
        "4.  Unzip the downloaded file (it will be named `yoga-poses-dataset.zip`). This will likely create a folder named `yoga_dataset_v1` or similar, containing `TRAIN` and `TEST` subdirectories.\n",
        "5.  Create a directory named `INPUT_DATASET` in the same directory as this notebook.\n",
