    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# **Step 2. Model Building**\n",
        "This part is where you construct your neural network. This typically involves selecting a base model, such as a pre-trained network like Xception, and customizing it by adding layers tailored to the specific task of yoga pose detection. The architecture is finalized with an output layer designed to classify the number of yoga poses we're focusing on."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "k5foekCSn0z_"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "# Building the model\n",
        "base_model = Xception(weights = 'imagenet', # Load weights from ImageNet\n",
        "                      include_top = False,\n",
        "                      input_shape = (300, 300, 3))\n",
        "\n",
        "model_layers = Sequential([\n",
        "    Flatten(input_shape = base_model.output_shape[1:]),\n",
        "    Dense(128, activation = 'relu'),\n",
        "    Dropout(0.2),\n",
        "    Dense(5, activation = 'softmax') # 5 classes for yoga poses\n",
        "])\n",
        "\n",
        "model = Model(inputs = base_model.input, outputs = model_layers(base_model.output))"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "LDa0zM2tn56w_updated"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# **Step 3. Model Training and Validation**\n",
        "This section involves compiling the model with appropriate loss functions, optimizers, and metrics, then training it using the prepared data. Concurrent validation ensures the model is learning effectively and not just memorizing the training data, a common problem known as overfitting."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "Fd0w8gKfoBPQ"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "# Compiling the model\n",
        "model.compile(optimizer=tf.keras.optimizers.SGD(learning_rate = 0.0001, momentum = 0.9, nesterov = True),\n",
        "              loss=tf.keras.losses.CategoricalCrossentropy(label_smoothing = 0.2, from_logits = False),\n",
        "              metrics=['accuracy'])\n",
        "\n",
        "model.summary()"
      ],
